+ Thought: 11.5s
Fixed. Here's what happened and what I did:
Root cause
Your AOC4 uploads weren't producing blank output randomly — every AOC4 task was crashing at pipeline start with No module named 'docx':
- automation_engine/modules/aoc4/parser.py imports python-docx at the top level
- Your server (/opt/anaconda3/bin/python3.13 running uvicorn) didn't have python-docx installed
- The crash left extracted_data empty → blank frontend wizard, and no Excel was ever generated
(All 7 tasks in your DB were stuck in error state with this exact log.)
Fixes applied
1. Installed python-docx into the anaconda environment your server runs on
2. Hardened parser.py:7-9 — the docx import is now optional/fault-tolerant, so even if the library goes missing again, AOC4 processing degrades gracefully instead of dying
Verified end-to-end
Ran the full ingest → extract → output pipeline against your uploaded KSPL files:
- 81 flags generated (38 common errors, 25 compliance, 18 RPT) → these now populate the frontend wizard
- Excel written: output/kp/kp_AOC4_Populated.xlsx with 166 populated cells across all 3 sheets
One note: both of your KSPL PDFs are scanned images (no text layer), so the Marker OCR stage does the heavy lifting — the Consolidated file already has cached OCR, but the Standalone one will be OCR'd fresh on first run (takes a few minutes, which is normal).
Just re-upload your document in the frontend (or re-process a task) and it should work now.